# The Vercel CLI does not read .gitignore. It has its own default exclusion list,
# and .gitignore is on it, which is easy to misread as "gitignored files are safe".
# They are not: anything on disk and not named here is uploaded and, if it sits
# under public/, served.
#
# Found the expensive way. The first production deployment published all 40 runs
# from this machine's local history, board and raw transcripts alike, across 12
# hosts, including failing grades against named third parties that this project
# deliberately does not publish. Four curated runs ship from examples/ instead, and
# that number is an editorial decision, not an accident of what was on disk.
public/runs

# Scratch probes. Outside public/, so never served, but no reason to upload them.
tmp
